cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "oss-profanity: profanity, emoji, and OSS code quality"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-04-25
authors:
  - family-names: Dubec
    given-names: Jakub
    email: jakub.dubec@stuba.sk
    affiliation: "Faculty of Informatics and Information Technologies, Slovak University of Technology in Bratislava"
url: "https://github.com/Sibyx/oss-profanity"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sibyx/oss-profanity"
keywords:
  - mining-software-repositories
  - github
  - gh-archive
  - profanity
  - emoji
  - code-quality
  - static-analysis
abstract: >-
  A research pipeline that mines one month of GH Archive data, scores
  profanity and emoji signals in commit messages and source comments,
  runs static analysers (ruff, lizard, bandit, jscpd, ESLint, tree-sitter)
  over a stratified cohort of repositories, and tests for correlation
  between each signal and common code-quality metrics.
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "Influence of profanity in commit messages on the quality of source code"
    authors:
